    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0194" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg90"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 2,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wharton acknowledges the receipt of Mr. Mizner’s telegram of the 1st instant,
                    and informs him that he was instructed on the 30th of August that Barrundia
                    entered the jurisdiction of Guatemala at his own risk, and it was for the
                    Guatemalan authorities to assume jurisdiction at their own responsibility and
                    risk; that the Department regretted his having advised or consented to the
                    surrender, particularly as violation of the ordinary laws of Guatemala was not
                    charged, and as the only allegation was that he was to be treated as an enemy
                    under martial law.</p>
